1
00:00:52,595 --> 00:00:53,471
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,596 --> 00:00:54,430
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:55,389
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:56,348
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:08,694
We can't.

6
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:13,324
I can't feel any more guilty
about Namgung.

7
00:01:19,622 --> 00:01:20,873
What about me?

8
00:01:24,919 --> 00:01:27,087
Are you okay
with feeling guilty toward me?

9
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:30,090
You said you liked that.

10
00:01:31,675 --> 00:01:35,137
You said making people feel guilty
is how you win their hearts.

11
00:01:48,317 --> 00:01:51,654
Get out. You're pissing me off.

12
00:03:04,727 --> 00:03:06,353
Go on in. It's late.

13
00:03:09,565 --> 00:03:11,150
And don't ever do this again.

14
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:16,864
Did you clean it?

15
00:03:16,989 --> 00:03:18,866
You have to, three times a day.

16
00:03:18,991 --> 00:03:20,159
Or it'll scar--

17
00:03:20,284 --> 00:03:22,286
Doing this won't change anything.

18
00:03:22,995 --> 00:03:25,372
It only puts Manager Eom at risk.

19
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:27,166
So stay out of this.

20
00:03:28,959 --> 00:03:30,461
Do you really want that?

21
00:03:32,129 --> 00:03:34,465
Do you really want me to stop?

22
00:03:35,591 --> 00:03:36,759
You don't, do you?

23
00:03:36,884 --> 00:03:38,177
You actually want me

24
00:03:38,844 --> 00:03:41,639
to fight to the end
more than anyone else, right?

25
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:45,976
You want me to do what you can't.
Am I wrong?

26
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:49,396
Yes, you're wrong.

27
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:52,816
I'm sick of ending things this way.

28
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,142
Where were you?

29
00:04:31,105 --> 00:04:33,440
How's rehab? Are you all done?

30
00:04:35,317 --> 00:04:37,152
Yes, they said it's fine.

31
00:04:40,531 --> 00:04:43,242
You can stay here until you find a place.

32
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:47,204
Is everything

33
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:49,790
okay at work?

34
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:54,920
You've been working late a lot lately.

35
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:57,172
Take care of yourself.

36
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:10,936
Why aren't you answering?

37
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:13,605
Are you crazy? You shouldn't be here.

38
00:05:13,731 --> 00:05:15,524
I said go, and you actually left?

39
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:17,943
Since when do you listen to me?

40
00:05:23,782 --> 00:05:25,576
You know I was just mad.

41
00:05:25,701 --> 00:05:29,163
You know I've got a shitty temper
and this is what I do.

42
00:05:29,288 --> 00:05:31,498
You know I didn't mean that!

43
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:34,877
Why can't you give in even once?

44
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:38,630
I give in to you nonstop.

45
00:05:39,506 --> 00:05:41,508
Why can't you give in just once?

46
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:45,971
Do you even like me at all?

47
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:49,516
You give in?

48
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:50,893
Don't I?

49
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:52,227
No, you don't.

50
00:05:54,021 --> 00:05:56,065
I'm the one who gives in to you.

51
00:05:58,067 --> 00:06:00,569
You give in? Like hell you do.

52
00:06:01,403 --> 00:06:02,654
Look at us now.

53
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,199
You can come whenever, but I can't.

54
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:09,328
I can't get mad
even when you cry over Namgung Ho!

55
00:06:09,453 --> 00:06:10,746
Tell me.

56
00:06:10,871 --> 00:06:12,831
When have you ever given in?

57
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:17,461
I'm still seeing you.

58
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:23,967
You asked whether I'd save
Namgung Ho or my dad,

59
00:06:25,177 --> 00:06:26,970
and I'm still seeing you.

60
00:06:30,641 --> 00:06:35,187
You tore open my deepest wound,
and I'm still seeing you.

61
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:40,776
I'm hurting someone
more precious than my life,

62
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:43,112
but I'm still seeing you.

63
00:07:14,977 --> 00:07:16,186
Move.

64
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:17,479
It's my fault.

65
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:21,316
I said it's my fault.

66
00:07:25,487 --> 00:07:26,905
No, it's not.

67
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:29,575
It's not her fault.

68
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:34,079
It's all my fault.

69
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:48,552
Hilarious.

70
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:53,640
Mi-do really is giving in.

71
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:53,909
ATTORNEY HAN TAE-SEUNG

72
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:25,941
12. WHO DO WE LOVE THE MOST?

73
00:09:27,109 --> 00:09:28,318
Are you okay?

74
00:09:29,319 --> 00:09:30,153
LEE MI-DO

75
00:09:30,279 --> 00:09:31,530
WHERE ARE YOU?

76
00:09:31,655 --> 00:09:32,990
PICK UP!

77
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:37,369
Is Namgung Ho always that hotheaded?

78
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:45,752
Oh.

79
00:09:48,005 --> 00:09:50,590
Why are you giving in to me?

80
00:09:50,716 --> 00:09:52,134
Yes?

81
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:55,554
Long time no see.

82
00:09:56,138 --> 00:09:58,974
Wow, it's shabbier than I thought.

83
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:01,393
Isn't it?

84
00:10:13,113 --> 00:10:17,284
Go ruin the Taegye-ri wind farm project.

85
00:10:19,911 --> 00:10:23,332
My father-in-law's district
desperately needs that project.

86
00:10:27,377 --> 00:10:28,462
I'm aware.

87
00:10:30,255 --> 00:10:33,258
Goyeong became the second choice
because of Taegye-ri, right?

88
00:10:35,761 --> 00:10:36,845
Oh.

89
00:10:37,721 --> 00:10:38,764
CEO Seo, or…

90
00:10:39,890 --> 00:10:40,807
Mr. Seo Ju-hyeok.

91
00:10:40,932 --> 00:10:44,186
I've been keeping tabs
on your father-in-law.

92
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,855
And I can guess why you're here.

93
00:10:50,859 --> 00:10:53,236
Taegye-ri is looking for a lawyer,

94
00:10:53,362 --> 00:10:55,322
and no one's better suited than you.

95
00:10:56,281 --> 00:10:58,200
Just talk them into registering a business

96
00:10:58,325 --> 00:11:00,952
to get proper land compensation.

97
00:11:01,078 --> 00:11:02,954
I'll handle the rest.

98
00:11:03,789 --> 00:11:05,624
It's so easy for you, isn't it?

99
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:08,919
Toss someone aside, pick them back up.

100
00:11:09,044 --> 00:11:10,379
I'm allowed to.

101
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:16,593
I'm allowed to do that.

102
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:26,812
Just show your cards.

103
00:11:27,771 --> 00:11:29,314
You didn't come for no reason.

104
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:32,901
About Director Lee Mi-do…

105
00:11:35,779 --> 00:11:36,863
How is she?

106
00:11:37,948 --> 00:11:38,824
You like her?

107
00:11:45,664 --> 00:11:46,665
I'm disappointed.

108
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:49,584
All you dug up is my love life?

109
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:52,170
And someone I only saw
out of boredom, at that.

110
00:11:53,755 --> 00:11:54,673
Nothing else?

111
00:11:54,798 --> 00:11:56,633
I'm the one who's disappointed.

112
00:11:57,926 --> 00:11:59,219
Tae-seung.

113
00:12:00,137 --> 00:12:01,388
You've been talking

114
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:04,307
way too much.

115
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,770
You should do what you're told.

116
00:12:22,451 --> 00:12:23,952
LEE SI-WOO, CORP. FINANCE 2

117
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:24,953
Yes, sir.

118
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,080
Hey.

119
00:12:28,081 --> 00:12:29,541
About Lee Mi-do's mother's place,

120
00:12:30,292 --> 00:12:31,751
as we discussed,

121
00:12:31,877 --> 00:12:35,714
file for demolition, restitution,
and damages.

122
00:12:36,506 --> 00:12:40,635
Attach the land encroachment survey
and apply for a provisional disposition.

123
00:12:41,386 --> 00:12:42,429
Oh, and earlier, I--

124
00:12:53,565 --> 00:12:55,066
The pacing drags too much.

125
00:12:55,192 --> 00:12:57,319
You said three minutes. I hit that.

126
00:12:57,444 --> 00:12:59,905
No, I meant
the first ten seconds drag too much.

127
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:01,281
-Really?
-Look, Director Lee.

128
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:03,533
Like I said, the B-roll is too long.

129
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:05,619
The viewer drop-off rate will skyrocket.

130
00:13:05,744 --> 00:13:07,078
This isn't a movie.

131
00:13:07,204 --> 00:13:08,997
Cutting shots won't help.

132
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:11,958
You need jump cuts here
to pick up the tempo.

133
00:13:13,585 --> 00:13:15,003
Never mind, we'll do it.

134
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:16,213
Yes, we'll do it.

135
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:27,557
We didn't mean it like that, Director Lee.

136
00:13:27,682 --> 00:13:29,309
We went too far. We're sorry.

137
00:13:29,434 --> 00:13:31,269
I didn't mean to sigh.

138
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:33,355
I just didn't sleep well.

139
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,649
It's okay. Call it out when needed.

140
00:13:36,441 --> 00:13:37,275
Yes.

141
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:39,945
Being harsh?

142
00:13:40,779 --> 00:13:41,821
That's fine.

143
00:13:41,947 --> 00:13:43,365
Better than not knowing.

144
00:13:44,866 --> 00:13:47,202
Your blatant attitude bugged me a bit,

145
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:51,790
but given how I treated you,
I'll let it slide as payback.

146
00:13:53,291 --> 00:13:55,043
As for the sigh,

147
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:57,254
I'll treat it as a bodily function.

148
00:13:58,547 --> 00:13:59,714
But…

149
00:14:02,634 --> 00:14:04,719
if you're going to teach me, do it right.

150
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,847
Properly. Like how I taught you guys.

151
00:14:07,973 --> 00:14:08,807
Okay?

152
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:13,728
Let's take five.

153
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:16,231
Feel free to badmouth me.

154
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:23,738
Why did you have to sigh?

155
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,615
Why did you talk like that?

156
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:38,211
TAK JACKSON

157
00:14:44,551 --> 00:14:46,803
Luc Mi-do, you still alive?

158
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:50,473
Are you avoiding me, too? Ghosting me?

159
00:14:51,308 --> 00:14:52,434
Traitor.

160
00:14:52,559 --> 00:14:54,853
Reaching three million tickets?
It's meaningless.

161
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,314
Oh, make that four million.

162
00:14:58,148 --> 00:15:00,358
I'm so bored and lonely.

163
00:15:02,861 --> 00:15:04,404
Isn't this your boyfriend's company?

164
00:15:07,741 --> 00:15:08,992
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

165
00:15:09,868 --> 00:15:14,289
HUNMIN CAUGHT SWAPPING
KOREAN SWEET POTATOES FOR CHEAP IMPORTS

166
00:15:18,293 --> 00:15:19,961
Did you see this article?

167
00:15:20,629 --> 00:15:21,463
What's this?

168
00:15:22,255 --> 00:15:23,131
Isn't this fake?

169
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:25,842
Things might get out of hand.

170
00:15:25,967 --> 00:15:27,594
The company didn't know this?

171
00:15:28,887 --> 00:15:30,680
Hello, this is Hunmin Confectionery.

172
00:15:30,805 --> 00:15:32,182
No, that report is false.

173
00:15:32,307 --> 00:15:34,017
-Internally…
-Please hold, sorry.

174
00:15:34,142 --> 00:15:34,976
Please hold…

175
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:36,227
Yes, as for returns…

176
00:15:36,353 --> 00:15:37,646
Yes, internally, we're…

177
00:15:39,648 --> 00:15:40,774
Is it not confirmed yet?

178
00:15:40,899 --> 00:15:42,609
Who's the whistleblower?

179
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:44,903
We're done. The stock's going to tank.

180
00:15:45,028 --> 00:15:46,237
Man, what do we do?

181
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:00,585
Is everything

182
00:16:02,545 --> 00:16:03,630
okay at work?

183
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:13,264
The number you have dialed
is not available.

184
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:15,767
Please leave a message after the tone…

185
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:19,104
You did this, right? I won't forgive you.

186
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:21,856
I will never, ever forgive you this time.

187
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,567
I'm going to the police. I'm suing--

188
00:16:24,693 --> 00:16:26,903
ASSISTANT MANAGER NAMGUNG

189
00:16:48,925 --> 00:16:50,218
ASSISTANT MANAGER NAMGUNG

190
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:58,309
Straight-up ignoring my calls, huh?

191
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:05,692
You got a death wish?

192
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:17,328
Still haven't found Pudgy a home?

193
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,330
I can already imagine.

194
00:17:20,123 --> 00:17:22,876
You were probably super picky
and rejected everyone.

195
00:17:24,085 --> 00:17:26,546
The company will put out
a rebuttal tomorrow.

196
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:29,340
The usual playbook.
Smear the whistleblower.

197
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:32,677
They'll say it was leaked for money,

198
00:17:33,428 --> 00:17:35,263
so the claims can't be trusted.

199
00:17:36,014 --> 00:17:37,599
Totally predictable.

200
00:17:37,724 --> 00:17:38,808
I didn't leak it.

201
00:17:39,768 --> 00:17:42,061
-I really didn't.
-I know it wasn't you.

202
00:17:46,274 --> 00:17:47,400
Who was it?

203
00:17:48,902 --> 00:17:50,361
Who took your files?

204
00:17:58,661 --> 00:18:00,705
The company already has

205
00:18:01,706 --> 00:18:03,458
records of payment from two outlets,

206
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:05,418
naming TF Team 3's Park Su-a,

207
00:18:06,377 --> 00:18:08,630
with proof confirming your ID.

208
00:18:08,755 --> 00:18:10,840
Unless something changes,

209
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,384
you're facing trade secret violations,

210
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,553
bribery, and ethics violations.

211
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:17,555
You'll face
the disciplinary panel tomorrow.

212
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:21,726
Then a police investigation.

213
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:25,146
So tell me.

214
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,775
You know who did it.

215
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:37,242
This is my mess.

216
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:40,078
I'll handle it.

217
00:18:40,203 --> 00:18:42,330
How are you going to handle it?

218
00:18:44,332 --> 00:18:46,668
Things are bad. Don't you get it?

219
00:18:46,793 --> 00:18:47,669
I do.

220
00:18:48,837 --> 00:18:50,880
I do, so please stay out of it.

221
00:18:54,801 --> 00:18:56,511
Manager Eom told me.

222
00:18:57,679 --> 00:18:59,305
The phone data wasn't recovered.

223
00:19:00,598 --> 00:19:02,809
You'll get in trouble
if you keep getting involved.

224
00:19:05,562 --> 00:19:06,396
And…

225
00:19:08,106 --> 00:19:10,024
I really couldn't bear that.

226
00:19:11,401 --> 00:19:12,569
So please…

227
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:16,281
Please stay out of it.

228
00:19:23,288 --> 00:19:25,540
I really thought I could do it.

229
00:19:26,374 --> 00:19:28,126
I really did.

230
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:29,794
But…

231
00:19:30,587 --> 00:19:32,171
I guess I was wrong.

232
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,176
I really was wrong.

233
00:19:58,156 --> 00:20:00,408
YEONG-DO

234
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:15,340
His vitals have all stabilized now.

235
00:20:15,465 --> 00:20:18,176
We need more tests for brain damage,

236
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,428
so be sure to get them done.

237
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:21,971
I see, thank you.

238
00:20:39,155 --> 00:20:41,324
Living like a corpse wasn't enough,

239
00:20:41,449 --> 00:20:44,118
so now you've got a death wish?

240
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:47,121
Even as a pro,
I'd black out once or twice a year.

241
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:48,331
It's no big deal.

242
00:20:48,456 --> 00:20:51,000
As for looking for Baek Bo-ra's
music box or whatever,

243
00:20:51,125 --> 00:20:52,418
tell me you'll stop now.

244
00:20:52,543 --> 00:20:54,420
Or I'm telling Mom everything.

245
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:55,546
I mean it.

246
00:20:56,172 --> 00:20:58,383
You want to turn Mom into a living corpse?

247
00:20:58,508 --> 00:20:59,425
You little punk!

248
00:20:59,550 --> 00:21:02,595
I left the ER less than two hours ago.

249
00:21:04,555 --> 00:21:05,598
Jeez.

250
00:21:07,016 --> 00:21:08,768
Why aren't you saying anything?

251
00:21:10,853 --> 00:21:11,854
Oh, Mi-do.

252
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,775
Mi-do, where are you going?

253
00:21:16,985 --> 00:21:18,027
Hey, Mi…

254
00:21:18,152 --> 00:21:18,987
Oh, shit.

255
00:21:23,866 --> 00:21:25,618
What?

256
00:21:25,743 --> 00:21:28,037
Help me out here! Ho!

257
00:21:31,582 --> 00:21:32,542
Tie him up!

258
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:34,836
I can't see! Ho, I can't see anything!

259
00:21:34,961 --> 00:21:35,837
Hit him, Mi-do!

260
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:43,511
Are you crazy?

261
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:45,304
No, cut it out!

262
00:21:45,430 --> 00:21:46,264
Are you insane?

263
00:21:47,223 --> 00:21:49,267
What are you doing? Stop it!

264
00:21:52,061 --> 00:21:53,938
Don't just watch! Stop her!

265
00:21:54,063 --> 00:21:56,649
Mi-do, stop! That's enough.

266
00:22:00,528 --> 00:22:03,281
You two live however you want,
so why can't I?

267
00:22:03,406 --> 00:22:04,824
Why can't I?

268
00:22:06,492 --> 00:22:08,578
Mi-do, why are you stopping?

269
00:22:08,703 --> 00:22:11,247
Beat him up more!
This bastard must be nuts.

270
00:22:11,372 --> 00:22:12,790
Go for it, Mi-do!

271
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:17,128
Say you'll never go in the water again.

272
00:22:22,508 --> 00:22:23,551
No.

273
00:22:26,304 --> 00:22:27,889
You little bastard!

274
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:31,601
He's your brother.

275
00:22:32,310 --> 00:22:34,020
Think this will make him listen?

276
00:22:46,324 --> 00:22:48,910
Only go on weekends, with me.

277
00:22:51,287 --> 00:22:53,623
Then I'll stop them from beating you up.

278
00:22:53,748 --> 00:22:54,957
Hey.

279
00:22:56,751 --> 00:22:58,044
Answer me.

280
00:23:06,344 --> 00:23:07,261
Okay.

281
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:35,456
Hey, Bo-ra!

282
00:23:36,541 --> 00:23:37,917
What are you doing here?

283
00:23:38,042 --> 00:23:39,252
I was so worried--

284
00:23:39,377 --> 00:23:40,753
You mean annoyed.

285
00:23:42,713 --> 00:23:43,673
What?

286
00:23:45,675 --> 00:23:46,884
Am I wrong?

287
00:23:48,970 --> 00:23:51,305
What do you mean? Stop accusing me.

288
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,432
Don't look at me like that.

289
00:23:53,558 --> 00:23:56,519
Don't look at me like you're sick of me.

290
00:24:01,858 --> 00:24:04,026
You shouldn't have saved me then.

291
00:24:04,694 --> 00:24:07,363
You should've just let me die.

292
00:24:10,199 --> 00:24:13,578
Then I'd remember you
as the Lee Wan-do who loved me.

293
00:24:18,124 --> 00:24:19,500
The music box…

294
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:23,713
I threw it into Seokchon Lake.

295
00:24:27,425 --> 00:24:28,426
You know, right?

296
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:32,555
That I can't sleep without it.

297
00:24:37,101 --> 00:24:39,061
When I die, make sure you find it.

298
00:24:41,898 --> 00:24:43,357
If you don't…

299
00:24:46,527 --> 00:24:49,113
I'll never rest because of you,
even in death.

300
00:25:06,714 --> 00:25:08,049
Bo-ra.

301
00:25:12,178 --> 00:25:14,472
Are you still unable to rest?

302
00:25:18,476 --> 00:25:20,144
Are you still not at peace…

303
00:25:23,814 --> 00:25:26,067
because of me?

304
00:26:00,685 --> 00:26:02,228
How many meters today?

305
00:26:04,855 --> 00:26:05,815
Two hundred meters.

306
00:26:06,482 --> 00:26:09,568
Or maybe 250.

307
00:26:12,113 --> 00:26:13,114
Sorry.

308
00:26:14,073 --> 00:26:15,449
I made you worry earlier.

309
00:26:17,368 --> 00:26:18,619
But look.

310
00:26:19,870 --> 00:26:21,122
I'm really struggling.

311
00:26:24,625 --> 00:26:25,835
It's just too hard.

312
00:26:29,213 --> 00:26:32,091
I tried to hold out until
the fifth anniversary of Bo-ra's death,

313
00:26:32,216 --> 00:26:33,676
but I can't do this anymore.

314
00:26:38,556 --> 00:26:40,349
Stop using Bo-ra as an excuse.

315
00:26:41,309 --> 00:26:42,560
Stop lying.

316
00:26:43,477 --> 00:26:46,188
After you had inner ear barotrauma
six years ago,

317
00:26:46,314 --> 00:26:48,316
your dive times got worse,
your ranking fell,

318
00:26:48,441 --> 00:26:50,609
and you never got your old form back.

319
00:26:51,569 --> 00:26:54,322
Right when you had to end
your athletic career,

320
00:26:54,447 --> 00:26:56,991
at your most hopeless moment, Bo-ra died.

321
00:27:02,038 --> 00:27:03,581
Sure, your feelings for her

322
00:27:04,415 --> 00:27:05,291
include guilt.

323
00:27:05,875 --> 00:27:08,419
That's part of it.
Of course it is. But Wan-do…

324
00:27:12,423 --> 00:27:15,134
If you're truly sorry for her,
don't live like this.

325
00:27:15,259 --> 00:27:17,303
She'd be so heartbroken.

326
00:27:18,596 --> 00:27:21,265
If she knew she's an excuse
to shut yourself away,

327
00:27:21,974 --> 00:27:23,684
it would break her heart.

328
00:27:45,539 --> 00:27:47,792
His CT and MRI came back normal.

329
00:27:51,796 --> 00:27:54,799
You know he won't stop
just because we tell him to.

330
00:27:54,924 --> 00:27:57,218
I'll take full responsibility for him,

331
00:27:57,802 --> 00:27:59,053
so don't worry.

332
00:28:01,347 --> 00:28:04,100
Are you really going to dive with Wan-do
on weekends?

333
00:28:05,142 --> 00:28:06,811
You know I'm certified.

334
00:28:08,521 --> 00:28:10,648
I'm not afraid of water like you.

335
00:28:14,819 --> 00:28:16,570
Because you gritted your teeth.

336
00:28:19,407 --> 00:28:20,574
All because of me.

337
00:28:22,118 --> 00:28:25,496
You were terrified,
but you pushed through it anyway.

338
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:30,584
When Wan-do first said
he wanted to swim,

339
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:32,670
and I agreed,

340
00:28:33,379 --> 00:28:35,673
you started swimming lessons that day.

341
00:28:37,758 --> 00:28:38,926
I know everything.

342
00:28:41,595 --> 00:28:42,430
Namgung.

343
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:46,100
You'd do anything for me.

344
00:28:47,518 --> 00:28:49,019
And I feel the same way.

345
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:52,940
But you know what?

346
00:28:58,112 --> 00:29:00,197
At least I lived for myself.

347
00:29:01,449 --> 00:29:02,616
Even with film,

348
00:29:03,451 --> 00:29:04,952
I did what I wanted

349
00:29:05,536 --> 00:29:07,955
and saw it through to the end.

350
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:12,918
But you never did.

351
00:29:22,803 --> 00:29:23,846
I take it back.

352
00:29:28,225 --> 00:29:30,811
I take back telling you…

353
00:29:34,106 --> 00:29:35,232
to stop liking her.

354
00:29:45,034 --> 00:29:46,035
Namgung.

355
00:29:49,497 --> 00:29:51,415
Do whatever you want.

356
00:29:55,085 --> 00:29:58,923
Whatever it is, whatever choice you make.

357
00:30:01,967 --> 00:30:03,677
Do whatever you want.

358
00:30:06,847 --> 00:30:09,099
Don't even think about me.

359
00:30:10,601 --> 00:30:11,644
Just…

360
00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:14,021
do it all.

361
00:30:25,282 --> 00:30:27,910
DAMUNGOL
THE WORST NOODLE SHOP IN TOWN

362
00:30:28,035 --> 00:30:30,329
ONLY TOTAL SUCKERS EAT HERE

363
00:30:30,454 --> 00:30:33,999
What are you going to do about this?

364
00:30:34,124 --> 00:30:36,502
I can't just let this slide.

365
00:30:36,627 --> 00:30:37,878
I apologize.

366
00:30:38,003 --> 00:30:40,172
I'll make sure it's repainted today.

367
00:30:40,297 --> 00:30:41,298
I'm so sorry.

368
00:30:42,049 --> 00:30:43,592
Why are you apologizing?

369
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:45,135
He started it…

370
00:30:47,555 --> 00:30:49,014
He insulted Mom!

371
00:30:49,557 --> 00:30:51,100
Called her a greedy tutor witch!

372
00:30:51,225 --> 00:30:52,351
Lee Sang-su.

373
00:30:55,521 --> 00:30:56,814
I apologize.

374
00:31:11,745 --> 00:31:13,247
Just go. I'll handle it.

375
00:31:14,582 --> 00:31:16,959
How? With a settlement?

376
00:31:19,086 --> 00:31:20,129
Mun-yeong.

377
00:31:22,506 --> 00:31:24,717
Do you remember the 47 vows

378
00:31:24,842 --> 00:31:26,385
I made when I proposed?

379
00:31:26,510 --> 00:31:29,138
With the sub-clauses, it was 52.

380
00:31:31,140 --> 00:31:32,558
Right, 52.

381
00:31:34,643 --> 00:31:38,439
I couldn't keep them all,
but I'll definitely keep this one.

382
00:31:40,941 --> 00:31:43,444
To be a good father to Sang-su.

383
00:31:46,822 --> 00:31:48,407
I'll definitely keep that.

384
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:57,082
Mun-yeong.

385
00:31:58,709 --> 00:32:00,127
Congrats on your marriage.

386
00:32:01,295 --> 00:32:02,338
Have a happy life.

387
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:06,050
I'm heading out.

388
00:32:16,685 --> 00:32:17,645
Hey…

389
00:32:18,479 --> 00:32:21,607
What? You want to know
if he treats me well? If I'm happy?

390
00:32:21,732 --> 00:32:23,651
No, that's not it. Just…

391
00:32:24,193 --> 00:32:25,861
check who the insurance beneficiary is.

392
00:32:26,779 --> 00:32:28,906
Why is such a young, handsome guy
dating you?

393
00:32:29,573 --> 00:32:31,158
Vet him before you marry him.

394
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:32,576
I can get a PI.

395
00:32:33,285 --> 00:32:34,787
Why, you little…

396
00:32:35,454 --> 00:32:36,705
Hey!

397
00:32:49,176 --> 00:32:54,348
BROTHER CLEANING

398
00:32:56,517 --> 00:32:59,353
Your mom was a really good teacher.

399
00:32:59,478 --> 00:33:01,480
If not for her irritable bowel syndrome,

400
00:33:02,022 --> 00:33:03,774
she'd have passed the certification exam.

401
00:33:06,068 --> 00:33:08,821
And your mom donates the most
among celebrity instructors.

402
00:33:08,946 --> 00:33:11,240
Almost as if her only son's
inheritance didn't matter.

403
00:33:13,659 --> 00:33:14,993
As long as you know.

404
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:17,538
Whatever people say about your mom,

405
00:33:17,663 --> 00:33:19,915
calling her money-crazy or whatever,

406
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:23,419
you just need to know she isn't like that.

407
00:33:23,544 --> 00:33:25,546
So we're just going to do nothing?

408
00:33:26,922 --> 00:33:30,634
Dad, I toned it down
because I didn't want to shock you.

409
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:34,680
I never said I'd do nothing.

410
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:37,224
Son.

411
00:33:37,808 --> 00:33:39,935
You should've called your dad for this.

412
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,229
And for this,

413
00:33:43,439 --> 00:33:45,065
you use industrial-grade.

414
00:33:46,275 --> 00:33:47,234
Got it?

415
00:33:54,074 --> 00:33:55,451
What do I put?

416
00:33:55,576 --> 00:33:57,119
"Beautiful Instructor Ko Mun-yeong."

417
00:33:57,828 --> 00:33:58,662
Got it.

418
00:34:01,415 --> 00:34:07,045
15 YEARS RUNNING…
BEAUTIFUL INSTRUCTOR…

419
00:34:13,135 --> 00:34:17,139
Why didn't you follow
the internal reporting procedures?

420
00:34:18,724 --> 00:34:20,267
I couldn't trust them.

421
00:34:22,144 --> 00:34:24,938
That is your subjective judgment.

422
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:29,735
Company policy dictates that matters
be handled through internal channels.

423
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:30,944
By your own rules,

424
00:34:31,987 --> 00:34:34,406
you should've investigated
the corruption suspects first.

425
00:34:35,157 --> 00:34:36,408
Regarding that,

426
00:34:36,950 --> 00:34:40,120
the audit team is currently
investigating the facts.

427
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:43,457
Then have you investigated me already?

428
00:34:47,628 --> 00:34:51,548
Did you check my attendance records
for the date and time

429
00:34:52,382 --> 00:34:55,594
the  Gangmu Daily  reporter
claimed I exchanged the files for money?

430
00:34:56,261 --> 00:34:58,180
How thoroughly
did you verify the possibility

431
00:34:58,764 --> 00:35:00,849
that the USB files given to reporters

432
00:35:00,974 --> 00:35:04,061
were fabricated
or leaked without authorization?

433
00:35:04,186 --> 00:35:07,231
DISCIPLINARY PANEL MEMBER, CHAIR

434
00:35:07,981 --> 00:35:10,567
I will not explain a single thing

435
00:35:10,692 --> 00:35:12,903
to this committee
with no procedural legitimacy.

436
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,906
If you want my explanation,

437
00:35:16,740 --> 00:35:19,201
do a proper investigation
by the rules first.

438
00:35:22,746 --> 00:35:23,997
It's for the best.

439
00:35:24,915 --> 00:35:27,042
Once I gathered all the files,

440
00:35:27,167 --> 00:35:30,337
I was going to offer them up
to an executive I trust

441
00:35:30,462 --> 00:35:32,256
and ride their coattails.

442
00:35:33,590 --> 00:35:35,092
But there's nobody I trust.

443
00:35:35,801 --> 00:35:38,220
Is having good character and competence

444
00:35:38,345 --> 00:35:40,055
while being squeaky clean really hard?

445
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:42,140
Man…

446
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:46,562
Forget it. It's over anyway, damn it.

447
00:35:49,439 --> 00:35:51,567
I told you
to just be a good dad to Su-min.

448
00:35:55,404 --> 00:35:57,531
That alone is a huge deal.

449
00:36:01,285 --> 00:36:04,746
I'm not that great of a dad to Su-min.

450
00:36:08,834 --> 00:36:11,086
Lately, I keep losing my temper

451
00:36:12,087 --> 00:36:13,380
at Su-min.

452
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:17,384
Who am I living like this for?

453
00:36:17,509 --> 00:36:20,262
I want to quit hundreds of times a day,

454
00:36:20,387 --> 00:36:22,890
but it's all for that piano
she loves so much…

455
00:36:27,394 --> 00:36:30,647
Then suddenly, I had a thought.

456
00:36:31,273 --> 00:36:34,651
"Did anyone tell me to live like this?"

457
00:36:37,779 --> 00:36:40,490
At this rate, I thought I might…

458
00:36:42,868 --> 00:36:46,705
really end up hating Su-min.

459
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:52,794
So, for one last time,
I wanted to do what I wanted.

460
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:54,212
Go all in on life.

461
00:36:54,338 --> 00:36:56,006
So I took the plunge, and…

462
00:36:57,215 --> 00:36:58,342
Damn it.

463
00:37:00,552 --> 00:37:03,597
I knew it'd happen, so no regrets.

464
00:37:04,932 --> 00:37:06,516
I'm glad. What a relief.

465
00:37:13,774 --> 00:37:15,150
I mean it.

466
00:37:15,901 --> 00:37:17,027
Such a relief.

467
00:37:24,618 --> 00:37:25,452
Fine!

468
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:27,704
Yes, I regret it, you bastard! Okay?

469
00:37:27,829 --> 00:37:29,456
Why didn't you stop me?

470
00:37:29,581 --> 00:37:32,000
You know how I get.
Why didn't you stop me?

471
00:37:32,125 --> 00:37:34,419
You have my wife's number.

472
00:37:34,544 --> 00:37:36,004
You could've called her, you brat!

473
00:37:36,129 --> 00:37:38,048
Why didn't you call?

474
00:37:39,383 --> 00:37:41,969
Why didn't you stop me? Why?

475
00:37:44,846 --> 00:37:46,348
Because I was rooting for you.

476
00:37:49,893 --> 00:37:51,186
I truly was.

477
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:56,066
Because I wanted you to make director.

478
00:38:16,962 --> 00:38:20,465
At least double the current payout!

479
00:38:20,590 --> 00:38:21,425
Double…

480
00:38:21,550 --> 00:38:22,384
COMMUNITY HALL

481
00:38:22,509 --> 00:38:23,385
So you mean,

482
00:38:23,510 --> 00:38:26,888
to get more than the land compensation,

483
00:38:27,014 --> 00:38:28,890
we need to register a business?

484
00:38:29,016 --> 00:38:30,142
Exactly.

485
00:38:30,267 --> 00:38:33,311
Sell it as forest land,
it's 20,000 won per 3.3 square meters.

486
00:38:33,437 --> 00:38:36,273
-Twenty thousand won.
-That only covers  makgeolli  and  pajeon.

487
00:38:36,398 --> 00:38:37,733
But as a business site,

488
00:38:38,775 --> 00:38:41,528
it's  makgeolli, pajeon,
and yellowtail sashimi!

489
00:38:41,653 --> 00:38:42,612
-Sashimi?
-Sashimi!

490
00:38:42,738 --> 00:38:46,283
On top of the land payout,
you'll get extra compensation

491
00:38:46,908 --> 00:38:48,577
such as structure and business losses.

492
00:38:49,536 --> 00:38:51,329
-Will it work?
-Okay.

493
00:38:51,455 --> 00:38:52,622
Sounds good,

494
00:38:52,748 --> 00:38:55,876
but if project costs go up
and another town snatches it,

495
00:38:56,001 --> 00:38:57,586
then what do we do?

496
00:38:57,711 --> 00:39:00,338
-Won't we be left empty-handed?
-Right.

497
00:39:01,048 --> 00:39:03,091
You don't need to worry about that.

498
00:39:03,216 --> 00:39:05,635
Now, here in Taegye-ri,

499
00:39:05,761 --> 00:39:09,389
the wind coming over the ridges
is steady all year round.

500
00:39:09,514 --> 00:39:11,683
-Right.
-A location like this--

501
00:39:11,808 --> 00:39:13,518
How do I get to the store?

502
00:39:17,731 --> 00:39:20,275
Go ahead and introduce yourselves.

503
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:23,904
This is the wonderful lawyer from Seoul

504
00:39:24,029 --> 00:39:26,740
who's helping with our wind farm.

505
00:39:27,407 --> 00:39:30,410
And she just came out here today

506
00:39:31,078 --> 00:39:33,997
on a spontaneous trip.
What did you say you do?

507
00:39:34,122 --> 00:39:35,457
-I'm unemployed.
-Unemployed.

508
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:40,420
Hello. I'm Lee Mi-do.

509
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,228
What's going on?

510
00:39:57,145 --> 00:39:57,979
Explain.

511
00:39:58,647 --> 00:40:01,233
Didn't you check the forecast?
No umbrella?

512
00:40:01,358 --> 00:40:05,487
Don't change the subject.
Tell me what's going on.

513
00:40:08,115 --> 00:40:10,909
I saw Seo Ju-hyeok
coming out of your office.

514
00:40:11,952 --> 00:40:12,994
Yes, sir.

515
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:13,954
Yes.

516
00:40:14,746 --> 00:40:16,873
I found a lawyer for Taegye-ri.

517
00:40:17,624 --> 00:40:19,584
Yes, you don't need to worry at all.

518
00:40:34,641 --> 00:40:36,101
I had no choice.

519
00:40:37,269 --> 00:40:39,437
Seo Ju-hyeok knows about you and me.

520
00:40:40,605 --> 00:40:42,607
I really didn't want to do it, either.

521
00:40:53,076 --> 00:40:54,911
I'll give you one last chance

522
00:40:56,329 --> 00:40:58,165
to tell the truth.

523
00:40:59,499 --> 00:41:03,170
Tae-seung, I know you
much better than you think.

524
00:41:03,295 --> 00:41:05,839
It's not something I wanted, but I do.

525
00:41:05,964 --> 00:41:07,757
So just be honest with me.

526
00:41:12,262 --> 00:41:14,139
Can you live in a place like this?

527
00:41:14,264 --> 00:41:19,227
How does it feel
to wake up and go to sleep

528
00:41:21,354 --> 00:41:22,522
in a place like this?

529
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:28,612
The man who put me in here
has no right to ask that.

530
00:41:28,737 --> 00:41:30,947
So I'm thinking of getting you out.

531
00:41:33,909 --> 00:41:35,493
What, you don't want me to?

532
00:41:38,622 --> 00:41:39,748
Tae-seung.

533
00:41:39,873 --> 00:41:41,750
You can't survive in here.

534
00:41:41,875 --> 00:41:42,751
I mean,

535
00:41:42,876 --> 00:41:45,712
you could never.

536
00:41:46,713 --> 00:41:47,881
You know why?

537
00:41:49,382 --> 00:41:51,885
Because I made you

538
00:41:52,636 --> 00:41:54,846
into someone who can't.

539
00:41:58,183 --> 00:41:59,100
Right?

540
00:42:07,817 --> 00:42:09,653
I can't let myself go to waste.

541
00:42:11,154 --> 00:42:13,698
I'm too good to just rot away like this.

542
00:42:15,033 --> 00:42:16,910
I know what it took to get here.

543
00:42:17,035 --> 00:42:19,746
I clawed like hell
to crawl out of that gutter.

544
00:42:21,790 --> 00:42:23,208
If I let this opportunity go,

545
00:42:25,293 --> 00:42:27,379
I might regret it my whole life.

546
00:42:31,007 --> 00:42:32,676
I'm really sorry,

547
00:42:35,220 --> 00:42:37,430
but I don't want to be like you.

548
00:42:39,349 --> 00:42:42,435
I don't want to lose this chance

549
00:42:43,144 --> 00:42:44,938
and feel the fear you feel.

550
00:42:52,946 --> 00:42:54,030
Leave.

551
00:42:56,074 --> 00:42:58,702
Whatever you say, I won't change my mind.

552
00:43:00,453 --> 00:43:01,496
Don't kid yourself.

553
00:43:03,331 --> 00:43:05,709
You think I came to persuade you?

554
00:43:05,834 --> 00:43:09,004
No. Seeing how you act
will kill any feelings I have left.

555
00:43:09,129 --> 00:43:10,130
That's why I came.

556
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:12,966
Seeing how vile you are up close,

557
00:43:13,091 --> 00:43:15,760
I'll be able to erase
every feeling I have left.

558
00:43:15,885 --> 00:43:17,137
That's why I'm here.

559
00:43:20,557 --> 00:43:21,516
We have four days.

560
00:43:22,976 --> 00:43:25,603
After that, I don't want to
remember a jerk like you.

561
00:43:27,188 --> 00:43:29,983
I refuse to remember
someone who's far more despicable

562
00:43:30,775 --> 00:43:32,193
than I ever imagined.

563
00:43:36,072 --> 00:43:37,532
I'm glad I came.

564
00:43:39,284 --> 00:43:40,618
It's good I came.

565
00:43:55,091 --> 00:43:56,551
I want to forget you, too!

566
00:43:58,470 --> 00:43:59,387
I'm the one

567
00:44:00,430 --> 00:44:03,391
who wants to completely forget
about someone like you, got that?

568
00:44:03,516 --> 00:44:04,517
Great.

569
00:44:05,185 --> 00:44:07,020
Then let's both try hard to forget.

570
00:44:07,145 --> 00:44:09,105
-Hey!
-Watch your tone!

571
00:44:12,275 --> 00:44:15,320
Watch your tone, Mr. Han Tae-seung.

572
00:45:38,736 --> 00:45:41,781
ASSISTANT MANAGER NAMGUNG

573
00:45:44,617 --> 00:45:45,910
Hey, Namgung Ho.

574
00:45:48,121 --> 00:45:49,456
Hello?

575
00:45:54,878 --> 00:45:57,380
I know you're listening.

576
00:46:00,258 --> 00:46:02,635
Are you really not coming?

577
00:46:05,180 --> 00:46:08,641
I even gave you my door code.

578
00:46:09,809 --> 00:46:12,812
The day we first met on Haemado.

579
00:46:13,855 --> 00:46:16,399
That's the door code.

580
00:46:17,859 --> 00:46:18,985
You…

581
00:46:19,736 --> 00:46:21,654
I warned you.

582
00:46:22,238 --> 00:46:24,824
Don't get involved in this.

583
00:46:27,160 --> 00:46:30,914
I know you feel for Manager Eom,

584
00:46:32,790 --> 00:46:35,043
but it's already too late for him.

585
00:46:35,877 --> 00:46:38,254
It's far too late.

586
00:46:38,922 --> 00:46:39,839
Hey.

587
00:46:41,216 --> 00:46:42,884
Are you listening?

588
00:46:43,885 --> 00:46:45,720
Yes, I'm listening.

589
00:46:49,390 --> 00:46:53,436
You're day drinking
just because you were placed on leave?

590
00:47:00,485 --> 00:47:02,654
Shut up, you apparition.

591
00:47:03,571 --> 00:47:07,534
Hey, Namgung, are you listening?

592
00:47:09,994 --> 00:47:12,330
How are you going to face me after this?

593
00:47:17,710 --> 00:47:20,880
I black out when I drink.

594
00:47:22,257 --> 00:47:25,635
I don't remember a single thing.

595
00:47:26,803 --> 00:47:28,304
I take after my dad.

596
00:47:30,306 --> 00:47:35,687
That's why he was always getting drunk
and causing trouble.

597
00:47:49,450 --> 00:47:51,202
Seven cans in total.

598
00:47:52,579 --> 00:47:53,413
After five cans,

599
00:47:54,455 --> 00:47:58,209
I completely black out.

600
00:48:00,628 --> 00:48:01,588
You sure?

601
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:03,923
Yes.

602
00:48:05,633 --> 00:48:09,012
That's why I only drink at home.

603
00:48:14,434 --> 00:48:15,518
Why?

604
00:48:16,769 --> 00:48:17,687
Jealous?

605
00:48:44,088 --> 00:48:45,214
What's this?

606
00:48:47,675 --> 00:48:49,761
Why does this feel so real?

607
00:48:52,513 --> 00:48:53,890
So annoying.

608
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:06,819
I really wanted to do this…

609
00:49:09,447 --> 00:49:11,449
at least once.

610
00:49:15,370 --> 00:49:16,537
Hey, you apparition.

611
00:49:17,330 --> 00:49:18,539
Let go.

612
00:49:20,416 --> 00:49:21,542
Hey!

613
00:49:23,795 --> 00:49:25,296
You did nothing wrong.

614
00:49:28,216 --> 00:49:30,968
So don't ever regret it.

615
00:49:35,807 --> 00:49:37,016
Great work.

616
00:49:39,185 --> 00:49:41,145
You really did an excellent job,

617
00:49:42,772 --> 00:49:44,023
Su-a.

618
00:50:44,333 --> 00:50:48,129
CALL RECORDING: ASSISTANT MANAGER NAMGUNG

619
00:50:48,254 --> 00:50:50,089
MOVE THIS RECORDING TO TRASH?

620
00:50:50,214 --> 00:50:51,591
ALL RECORDINGS

621
00:51:33,424 --> 00:51:34,967
What? I'm fine.

622
00:51:48,189 --> 00:51:49,273
Mi-do.

623
00:51:51,818 --> 00:51:54,028
Don't forget me too quickly.

624
00:51:55,363 --> 00:51:57,156
And don't forget everything.

625
00:51:59,659 --> 00:52:02,495
I'm really sorry I'm like this.

626
00:52:05,832 --> 00:52:07,166
But ten days a year…

627
00:52:08,125 --> 00:52:09,168
No.

628
00:52:10,837 --> 00:52:11,712
A week.

629
00:52:13,756 --> 00:52:14,757
Actually, no.

630
00:52:18,010 --> 00:52:20,555
Even three days is enough.

631
00:52:23,266 --> 00:52:24,809
Just think of me sometimes.

632
00:52:28,855 --> 00:52:33,234
Otherwise, it'll feel so unfair.

633
00:52:50,167 --> 00:52:51,294
Hey!

634
00:53:12,648 --> 00:53:14,775
More often than just sometimes…

635
00:53:17,695 --> 00:53:22,450
Maybe I'll think of you
way more often than sometimes.

636
00:53:28,247 --> 00:53:30,207
Just promise me one thing.

637
00:53:34,587 --> 00:53:39,425
Don't make me regret
having feelings for you.

638
00:53:43,179 --> 00:53:44,305
Please,

639
00:53:45,389 --> 00:53:46,432
Tae-seung.

640
00:54:24,595 --> 00:54:25,763
Wash up while I heat this.

641
00:54:26,347 --> 00:54:27,348
We have somewhere to go.

642
00:54:29,934 --> 00:54:32,269
I found where Ji Su-yeon is.

643
00:54:34,271 --> 00:54:35,773
I'll go with you.

644
00:54:58,421 --> 00:54:59,922
It's a misunderstanding.

645
00:55:00,047 --> 00:55:02,216
I happened to see
the files on your laptop,

646
00:55:02,341 --> 00:55:04,468
and as a Hunmin Confectionery customer,

647
00:55:04,593 --> 00:55:07,221
I thought the public needed to know.

648
00:55:08,055 --> 00:55:11,976
You were torn
about blowing the whistle, weren't you?

649
00:55:12,101 --> 00:55:13,853
But that's wrong, isn't it?

650
00:55:13,978 --> 00:55:16,856
I know you work for them,
but people have a right to know.

651
00:55:19,150 --> 00:55:23,362
Su-a, when it really matters,
you only think of yourself.

652
00:55:24,238 --> 00:55:25,364
You're selfish.

653
00:55:26,574 --> 00:55:27,700
I'm selfish?

654
00:55:30,286 --> 00:55:33,289
You always say I'm selfish.

655
00:55:35,583 --> 00:55:37,501
-Aren't you?
-No, I'm not.

656
00:55:38,627 --> 00:55:40,755
I actually knew all along.

657
00:55:41,630 --> 00:55:43,424
But you meant so much to me,

658
00:55:44,425 --> 00:55:46,552
so I kept pretending not to know,

659
00:55:46,677 --> 00:55:49,138
just so we could stay friends.

660
00:55:50,514 --> 00:55:51,891
Why did we…

661
00:55:53,893 --> 00:55:55,394
end up like this?

662
00:55:57,021 --> 00:55:58,731
Who made me end up this way?

663
00:55:58,856 --> 00:55:59,940
You did.

664
00:56:00,608 --> 00:56:03,402
You're living like this
because of yourself, not me.

665
00:56:03,527 --> 00:56:05,738
Su-a.

666
00:56:05,863 --> 00:56:07,490
All that trash of yours.

667
00:56:09,909 --> 00:56:11,368
Stop dumping it on me.

668
00:56:13,996 --> 00:56:15,122
It's all yours.

669
00:56:20,961 --> 00:56:22,546
You'll hear from the police.

670
00:56:23,255 --> 00:56:25,883
I filed charges
for accessing and leaking files.

671
00:56:32,014 --> 00:56:33,557
You think you're so great.

672
00:56:33,682 --> 00:56:36,143
Always acting so smart,
principled, and moral.

673
00:56:36,977 --> 00:56:39,230
Do you know how suffocating it is
to be around you?

674
00:56:39,814 --> 00:56:44,235
You make everyone else look bad
just to protect yourself.

675
00:56:44,360 --> 00:56:46,320
That's why your dad left you.

676
00:56:46,987 --> 00:56:48,864
Because you disgusted him.

677
00:56:57,915 --> 00:56:59,041
Are you done?

678
00:57:01,210 --> 00:57:02,878
Keep going if you're not.

679
00:57:03,587 --> 00:57:04,547
I'll listen.

680
00:57:06,966 --> 00:57:08,050
Su-yeon.

681
00:57:08,884 --> 00:57:10,386
You didn't leave

682
00:57:11,804 --> 00:57:13,597
the slightest scratch on me.

683
00:57:15,057 --> 00:57:16,725
Because of you,

684
00:57:17,768 --> 00:57:19,436
I've grown to love myself more.

685
00:57:20,646 --> 00:57:24,650
Because of you, I'll probably be sad,
hurt, and struggling for a long time.

686
00:57:27,194 --> 00:57:28,737
But even so,

687
00:57:29,947 --> 00:57:31,824
I won't change myself for you.

688
00:57:33,993 --> 00:57:35,828
Because I wasn't wrong.

689
00:57:37,163 --> 00:57:38,497
I was right.

690
00:57:41,542 --> 00:57:43,335
I'll live a better life than anyone.

691
00:57:45,254 --> 00:57:46,589
I'll be happy.

692
00:58:08,319 --> 00:58:10,029
I handled it well.

693
00:58:11,197 --> 00:58:12,489
I know. I saw.

694
00:58:15,492 --> 00:58:16,577
You were watching?

695
00:58:16,702 --> 00:58:17,995
Yes.

696
00:58:19,079 --> 00:58:20,372
You're so mean.

697
00:58:20,497 --> 00:58:22,833
Why were you watching? You're so weird.

698
00:58:24,543 --> 00:58:26,295
I thought you'd look cool.

699
00:58:27,004 --> 00:58:29,006
And you really did.

700
00:58:32,092 --> 00:58:33,135
Su-a.

701
00:58:37,514 --> 00:58:40,059
Because of you,
I've grown to love myself more.

702
00:58:44,480 --> 00:58:45,773
So thank you.

703
00:58:49,109 --> 00:58:50,694
And fantasies do exist.

704
00:58:52,071 --> 00:58:53,072
Except,

705
00:58:54,698 --> 00:58:57,201
every fantasy is a long story.

706
00:59:05,084 --> 00:59:08,462
HINES OFFICETEL

707
00:59:08,629 --> 00:59:09,838
Assistant Manager Namgung.

708
00:59:13,092 --> 00:59:15,177
Is it really okay?

709
00:59:19,056 --> 00:59:20,266
If I…

710
00:59:22,184 --> 00:59:23,519
don't regret it?

711
00:59:28,357 --> 00:59:30,234
Were you lying to me?

712
00:59:32,486 --> 00:59:34,655
I usually don't remember.

713
00:59:34,780 --> 00:59:36,198
I really don't.

714
00:59:37,199 --> 00:59:39,201
But maybe because you pinched me…

715
00:59:41,203 --> 00:59:42,496
I'm annoyed, too.

716
00:59:45,874 --> 00:59:47,918
Then keep pretending you don't remember.

717
00:59:52,631 --> 00:59:54,216
I'll pretend I don't.

718
00:59:55,676 --> 00:59:57,052
But let's make eye contact.

719
00:59:59,596 --> 01:00:01,515
We only have three days left.

720
01:00:06,729 --> 01:00:07,604
Go ahead.

721
01:00:31,170 --> 01:00:32,171
Me too.

722
01:00:34,673 --> 01:00:36,216
Thanks to you,

723
01:00:37,217 --> 01:00:39,511
I've grown to love myself more, too.

724
01:00:43,182 --> 01:00:44,141
Thank you.

725
01:02:31,874 --> 01:02:34,001
15 YEARS RUNNING,
STUDENT SATISFACTION RATE

726
01:02:34,168 --> 01:02:35,752
BEAUTIFUL INSTRUCTOR KO MUN-YEONG

727
01:02:35,878 --> 01:02:38,130
TAEGYE-RI YOUNG ADULTS' ASSOCIATION

728
01:02:38,255 --> 01:02:39,756
THANK YOU TO SEO JIN-WON
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

729
01:02:39,882 --> 01:02:41,425
Let's form an alliance.

730
01:02:41,550 --> 01:02:43,677
How about a strategic approach?

731
01:02:43,802 --> 01:02:46,388
Lee Mi-do is seeing that lawyer punk
from his army days,

732
01:02:46,513 --> 01:02:48,682
and he's dating a junior at work.

733
01:02:48,807 --> 01:02:50,559
There's not been a single moment

734
01:02:50,684 --> 01:02:53,770
when I've been happy. You know that?

735
01:02:53,896 --> 01:02:55,772
You're starting to fall for me, right?

736
01:02:55,898 --> 01:02:57,566
Then keep falling for me.

737
01:02:57,691 --> 01:02:58,984
You did nothing wrong.

738
01:02:59,693 --> 01:03:01,778
It's all my fault.
